Client-side cold-vs-warm latency measurement for the PolyKernel Modal service.
Sleeps past scaledown_window to force a scale-down, times the first (cold) vs
subsequent (warm) requests, and writes reports/cold_start.json. Needs a
deployed app URL for a live run.
options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --url URL             deployed app base URL, e.g.
                        https://<app>--<env>.modal.run (omit with --dry-run
                        for a documented placeholder)
  --scaledown-window SCALEDOWN_WINDOW
                        app scaledown_window in seconds; the script sleeps
                        this + --margin to force scale-down (min 2s for the
                        fast negative case; default 300)
  --margin MARGIN       extra seconds slept past the scaledown window (default
                        5.0)
  --endpoint ENDPOINT   probe path (body-less GET recommended; default
                        /kernels)
  --repeat REPEAT       number of warm samples; warm_ms is their median
                        (default 3)
  --timeout TIMEOUT     per-request HTTP timeout in seconds (default 600.0)
  --dry-run             write a documented placeholder JSON without hitting
                        any URL (no token / no deployment needed)
  --out OUT             output JSON path (default reports/cold_start.json)

