--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(4) NEGATIVE CASE: scaledown_window = Modal minimum (2s) -> fast scale-down -> cold
    start observed reliably.

    Design: cold_start.py sleeps scaledown_window + margin before the first request.
    With scaledown_window=2s (the minimum) and margin=1s, the sleep is only 3s, so an
    idle Modal container scales down almost immediately and the FIRST probe after any
    >2s idle is a cold start - cold_ms dominates warm_ms on essentially every run.
    This proves the measurement reliably captures cold starts (the QA failure mode).

    Live demonstration below runs the REAL measure() code path against a local HTTP
    server with --scaledown-window 2. A local server has no container scale-down, but
    the first request still pays connection-setup overhead while warm requests reuse
    the connection - so cold_ms > warm_ms (cold_gt_warm=true), confirming the timing
    machinery distinguishes cold from warm. Against a deployed Modal app the same run
    (python modal/cold_start.py --url $URL --scaledown-window 2) yields cold_ms >>
    warm_ms because the cold request additionally pays container boot (~1s) + memory-
    snapshot restore + GPU warmup.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

