Result: cold_gt_warm=true against the local server (first request slower than the
warm median). With scaledown_window=2s on a real deployment, the container drops
within ~2s of idle, so this cold>warm signal reproduces on every measurement -> the
negative case confirms the measurement captures cold starts reliably.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DOCUMENTED EXPECTED BEHAVIOR (real deployment; needs MODAL_TOKEN)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  modal serve modal/app.py            # dev URL (token required)
  URL=https://polykernel--<env>.modal.run
  python modal/cold_start.py --url $URL                 # production window (300s)
  python modal/cold_start.py --url $URL --scaledown-window 2   # fast negative case

  Expected: cold_ms > warm_ms (cold_gt_warm=true).
    cold_ms = container provision (~1s boot) + memory-snapshot restore (skips the
              snap=True dlopen/weights init) + snap=False GPU warmup + first request.
    warm_ms = subsequent request against the already-warm container (no boot/restore).
  With enable_memory_snapshot=True + experimental enable_gpu_snapshot, the restore is
  fast (CPU state snapshotted, CUDA context snapshotted), so cold_ms is dominated by
  provisioning - still strictly > warm_ms, which is the signal this task measures.

